==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|offenen}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|gmh|offanōn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*upanōną}}. Compare {{cog|nl|openen}} and English [[open]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʔœfnən/|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|öff|nen|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-öffnen.ogg|audio (Germany)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-öffnen.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|öffnet|öffnete|geöffnet}}

# to [[open]]
#: {{ux|de|Das Kind '''öffnete''' die Fenster.|t=The child '''opened''' the windows.}}

====Usage notes====
While ''öffnen'' isn't explicitly formal, it is fairly infrequent in everyday spoken language, typically replaced by the colloquial ''[[aufmachen]]''

